% The SDK's skeleton: an asset its owner gives away
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% (InsurLE2/migration/daml) from its source (kept in sources/): each template a fluent keyed by
% the contract id, each create and choice an action, who may do what integrity constraints.
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the Legal View (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program).

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 5.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the asset *an asset* with issuer *an issuer*, owner *an owner* and name *a name*; known as create_asset.
    *a party* archives the asset *an asset*; known as archive_asset.
    *a party* exercises give on the asset *an asset* with new owner *a new owner* creating *a second asset*; known as give.

the fluents are:
    *an asset* is an asset with issuer *an issuer*, owner *an owner* and name *a name*; known as asset.

the knowledge base skeleton includes:

the text of "the source main/daml/Main.daml" is at "sources/main/daml/Main.daml".

the text of "the source test/daml/Test.daml" is at "sources/test/daml/Test.daml".

% Asset: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the asset an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
then the asset is an asset with issuer the issuer, owner the owner and name the name.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the asset an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the asset an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
    and the name is equal to "".

it must not be true that
    a party creates the asset an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
    and the asset is an asset with issuer a second issuer, owner a second owner and name a second name.

% Asset: archiving one (Daml's Archive choice) is for its signatories, and it must be active
when a party archives the asset an asset
    and the asset is an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
then it is not the case that the asset is an asset with issuer the issuer, owner the owner and name the name.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the asset an asset
    and the asset is an asset with issuer an issuer, owner an owner and name a name
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the asset an asset
    and it is not the case that the asset is an asset with issuer a thing, owner a second thing and name a third thing.

% Asset.Give (consuming): the controller (owner) must submit it, and the contract must be active
when a party exercises give on the asset an asset with new owner an owner creating a second asset
    and the asset is an asset with issuer an issuer, owner a second owner and name a name
then the second asset is an asset with issuer the issuer, owner the owner and name the name
    and it is not the case that the asset is an asset with issuer the issuer, owner the second owner and name the name.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises give on the asset an asset with new owner an owner creating a second asset
    and the asset is an asset with issuer an issuer, owner a second owner and name a name
    and the party is different from the second owner.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises give on the asset an asset with new owner an owner creating a second asset
    and it is not the case that the asset is an asset with issuer a thing, owner a second thing and name a third thing.

it must not be true that
    a party exercises give on the asset an asset with new owner an owner creating a second asset
    and the asset is an asset with issuer an issuer, owner a second owner and name a name
    and the name is equal to "".

% Daml (the script run on a Canton sandbox) ends with these active contracts (their payloads;
% the ids are the ledger's):
%   - asset(alice,alice,"TV")
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_daml.pl.
scenario setup is:
    % the Daml Script setup
    alice creates the asset alice_tv with issuer alice, owner alice and name "TV" from 1 to 2.
    alice exercises give on the asset alice_tv with new owner bob creating bob_tv from 2 to 3.
    bob exercises give on the asset bob_tv with new owner alice creating c1 from 3 to 4.

